  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A circle is inscribed in a triangle with sides \\(8,\\) \\(15,\\) and \\(17.\\) The radius of the circle is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(7\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": "3"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1955-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because \\(8^2+15^2=17^2,\\) the triangle is right. Its inradius is \\[ r=\\frac{8+15-17}{2}=3. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "The side lengths form a Pythagorean triple",
        "For a right triangle, \\(r=\\frac{a+b-c}{2}\\)"
      ],
